<DocsLayout title="Checkpoints" activeSlug="checkpoints" description="Checkpoints snapshot PAS-Agent task state, git state, and changed files at a point in time.">
  <h1>Checkpoints</h1>

  <p>
    Checkpoints are snapshots of your session at a specific point in time.
    They record the full task state, the git state, and which files had uncommitted changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Creating a Checkpoint</h2>
  <pre><code>$ pas-agent checkpoint "Implemented login endpoint"
Checkpoint #3 saved: Implemented login endpoint
  Files with uncommitted changes: 4</code></pre>
  <p>Each checkpoint records:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A message describing the milestone</li>
    <li>The current git branch and commit</li>
    <li>Files with uncommitted changes (staged, unstaged, and untracked), each marked as added, modified, deleted, renamed, or untracked</li>
    <li>A snapshot of the full task state</li>
    <li>A timestamp</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Listing Checkpoints</h2>
  <pre><code>$ pas-agent list
Checkpoints for my-project (3):
    1. 2026-09-17 04:30:00 UTC  Set up project structure  (6 files)  [abc1234d]
    2. 2026-09-17 04:35:12 UTC  Implemented login endpoint  (3 files)  [abc1234d]
    3. 2026-09-17 04:39:40 UTC  Added password hashing  (1 file)  [9f8e7d6c]</code></pre>

  <h2>How Checkpoints Are Used</h2>
  <p>
    When you export, the context file includes the most recent checkpoints and the files
    changed at the latest one:
  </p>
  <pre><code>## Files Changed (as of last checkpoint)
- `src/auth/hash.rs` (untracked)
- `src/auth/mod.rs` (modified)

## Checkpoint History
- **2026-09-17 04:30 UTC** — Set up project structure
- **2026-09-17 04:35 UTC** — Implemented login endpoint
- **2026-09-17 04:39 UTC** — Added password hashing</code></pre>
  <p>
    To keep context files small, only the last 10 checkpoints and 50 files are exported.
    Some agents limit how much of an instruction file they load. The full history
    stays in <code>session.json</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Checkpoints are stored inside <code>.pas-agent/session.json</code>, in order.
    Checkpoints taken in quick succession are all kept.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
